Hello Andrew.

Thank you again for the reply --- which makes perfect sense! This model is a bit quirky in this regard, but in any case...

I took your suggestion on board, and fiddling with the code a bit (i.e., making the edge cases explicit), I was able get it to run, and return sensible values (i.e., posteriors that included the values used to generate the simulated data), mirroring the optim results.

I am sure there is a much more efficient way of writing it, but this will do for now.

learn_hpois <- function(data, lower_N = 0, upper_N = 20, iter = 2000, warmup = 1000, chains = 4) {
  K <- seq( lower_N, upper_N )
  data_list <- list(
                     n_points = length( K ),
                     n_ind = nrow( data ),
                     n_detections = data$w,
                     n_samples = data$n_samples,
                     K = K)
  hpois_model <- '
  data{
    int<lower=1> n_points; //
    int<lower=1> n_ind; // number of surveyed birds
    int<lower=0> n_detections[n_ind]; // vector of number of detections
    int<lower=1> n_samples[n_ind]; // vector of number of tests
    int K[n_points];
  }
  parameters{
    real<lower=0> lambda; // distribution of abundance
    real<lower=0, upper=1> p_detect; // detection probability
  }
  model{

    real ps;
    real theta;
    real diff;
    int tmp_d;
    int tmp_n;

    lambda ~ exponential(1); // prior on lambda
    p_detect ~ uniform(0, 1); // flat prior on detection prob
    diff = (1 - p_detect);
    for(i in 1:n_ind) {

      tmp_d = n_detections[i];
      tmp_n = n_samples[i];
      ps = 0;

      for(j in 1:n_points) {
        theta = (1 - pow( diff, K[j] ));

        if( theta > 0 && theta < 1 ) {
           ps = ps + exp(poisson_lpmf(K[j] | lambda) + binomial_lpmf( tmp_d | tmp_n, theta ) );
        } else if( theta == 0 && tmp_d == 0 ) {
          ps = ps + exp(poisson_lpmf(K[j] | lambda) );
        } else if( theta == 1 && tmp_d == tmp_n ) {
          ps = ps + exp(poisson_lpmf(K[j] | lambda) );
        } else {
          ps = ps + 0;
        }
//        if( tmp_d == 0){
//          print("lambda= ", lambda," p_detect= ", p_detect, " ps=", ps, " n_detections=", tmp_d, " theta=", theta, " K=", K[j]);
//        }
      }
      target += log(ps);

    }
  }
  generated quantities {
    real psi; // probability of occupancy
    psi = 1 - exp( -lambda );
  }
  '
  fit <- rstan::stan( model_code = hpois_model,
                      data = data_list,
                      iter = iter,
                      warmup = warmup,
                      chains = chains)
  return( fit )
}

Thanks again.

Anders.

