I tried to warn about this earlier — taking real<lower = - pi() / 2, upper = pi() / 2> theta;
pushes a huge amount of probability mass at the discontinuity to infinity which the
sampler will have difficulty reaching in a reasonable amount of time.  I’m not sure
how this would exactly manifest, but it ultimately reduces to the fact that our HMC
sampler can only handle spaces that are globally homeomorphic to R^{n}.

