messages.body_plain:
Yes, your mentioning it and realizing that there are values near
the boundaries when I simulated is what led me to point it out.

I want to try the parameterization with

  parameters {
    unit_vector[2] xy;  // xy[1]^2 + xy[2]^2 = 1

  transformed parameters {
    real<lower=-pi()/2, upper=pi()/2> theta;
    theta = atan2(xy[1], xy[2]) - pi();

and see if that works.  The underlying unit vector
parameterization involves two parameters with an implicit
prior for identification.

- Bob

